WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
In the previous video, we saw what a LAN is. You know, a network which can span

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.719
across a small region. Now imagine you
want to connect devices across multiple

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:12.750
cities or multiple continents.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.609
Now, that's a huge network and that kind
of network is called WAN. In this, to

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:18.539
explain this,

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:21.750
let's take an example of an office
campus: you can have multiple buildings,

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.609
you know, multiple floors, you have
multiple computers in this different

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.900
floors. So, how do you connect them? You
take a router and put it in each floor

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.130
connect all the computers in in that
flow to the particular router and you

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.420
take a bigger router and you can all of
your router's to that and that's how you

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.430
can create a small WAN.

